    <h2>Discover the Flavors of Indonesia</h2>
    <h3>Soto Ayam: A Traditional Indonesian Delight</h3>
    
    <p>Soto ayam adalah makanan khas Indonesia berupa sup ayam berkuah kuning atau bening yang kaya akan rempah. Hidangan ini biasanya disajikan dengan nasi, soun, telur rebus, dan taburan bawang goreng.</p>
    
    <blockquote>
        <p><q>The secret to delicious Soto Ayam lies in the rich combination of aromatic spices and flavorful chicken broth.</q></p>
        <footer>- Indonesian Culinary Tradition</footer>
    </blockquote>
    
    <h3>Ingredients:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Chicken:</strong> 500g</li>
        <li><strong>Lemongrass:</strong> 2 stalks</li>
        <li><strong>Kaffir Lime Leaves:</strong> 3 leaves</li>
        <li><strong>Turmeric:</strong> 2 cm</li>
        <li><strong>Ginger:</strong> 2 cm</li>
        <li><strong>Garlic:</strong> 4 cloves</li>
        <li><strong>Shallots:</strong> 5 cloves</li>
        <li><strong>Vermicelli:</strong> 100g</li>
        <li><strong>Boiled Eggs:</strong> 2 eggs</li>
        <li><strong>Salt and Pepper:</strong> To taste</li>
    </ul>
    
    <h3>Preparation:</h3>
    <ol>
        <li><em>Boil the chicken in water until tender and the broth becomes flavorful.</em></li>
        <li><em>Grind the turmeric, ginger, garlic, and shallots into a spice paste.</em></li>
        <li><em>Sauté the spice paste until fragrant, then add lemongrass and kaffir lime leaves.</em></li>
        <li><em>Add the sautéed spices to the chicken broth and simmer for 15 minutes.</em></li>
        <li><em>Remove the chicken, shred the meat, and return it to the broth if desired.</em></li>
        <li><em>Season with salt and pepper to taste.</em></li>
        <li><em>Serve the soup with vermicelli, boiled eggs, and fried shallots.</em></li>
    </ol>
    
    <h3>Cooking Tips:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><sup>1</sup> teaspoon of ground coriander can enhance the traditional flavor.</li>
        <li><sub>1</sub> tablespoon of fried shallots adds a delicious aroma and texture.</li>
        <li>Serve with lime wedges and sambal for extra flavor.</li>
    </ul>
    
